---
import Layout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const lastUpdated = "August 19, 2026";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | Time Reminder"
  description="How Time Reminder collects, uses, and protects your data, including Google Analytics, Google AdSense, and Amazon affiliate links."
>
  <a class="skip-link" href="#main-content">Skip to privacy policy</a>
  <main id="main-content" class="page-shell privacy-page">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="intro">
      This policy explains what information Time Reminder collects, why we
      collect it, and the choices you have. We keep it plain on purpose.
    </p>
    <p class="updated-note">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <section aria-labelledby="who">
      <h2 id="who">Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        Time Reminder is a free browser tool that provides audible reminders at
        regular points throughout the hour. In this policy, "we," "us," and
        "Time Reminder" refer to the operator of this site.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Data controller:</strong> Time Reminder.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Contact:</strong> You can reach us through our
        <a href="/contact">Contact page</a> or at
        <a href="mailto:hello@timeremind.info">hello@timeremind.info</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="collect">
      <h2 id="collect">Information we collect</h2>
      <p>We collect only what we need to run the site and improve it.</p>

      <h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
      <p>
        When you visit Time Reminder, our analytics and advertising partners and
        we automatically collect some technical and usage information,
        including:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>IP address and approximate location (country or region)</li>
        <li>Browser type, device type, operating system, and language</li>
        <li>
          Pages and guides you view, and how you use the timer (for example,
          which tea and method you select and when you start a timer)
        </li>
        <li>Referring site, date and time of visit, and session duration</li>
        <li>
          Cookie and advertising identifiers, and (for personalized ads)
          inferred interests used to show relevant advertising
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        This is collected through Google Analytics and Google AdSense, as
        described below.
      </p>

      <h3>Information you give us directly</h3>
      <p>
        If you contact us, we may receive the information you choose to include
        in your message so we can read and reply to you.
      </p>

      <h3>Information from affiliate links</h3>
      <p>
        Some pages include Amazon affiliate links (see "Affiliate links" below).
        When you click one of those links, Amazon may set cookies and collect
        information under Amazon's own privacy policy. We do not receive your
        personal information from Amazon; we only receive a commission when a
        qualifying purchase is made.
      </p>

      <h3>What we do not collect</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>We do not create user accounts or require registration.</li>
        <li>
          We do not collect payment information; any purchase happens on Amazon
          or another retailer's site.
        </li>
        <li>
          We do not knowingly collect special-category data (such as health or
          biometric data).
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="how-collect">
      <h2 id="how-collect">How we collect information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Directly from you:</strong> information you choose to send through
          our contact page or email.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Automatically:</strong> cookies, similar technologies, and analytics
          scripts that load when you use the site.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>From third parties:</strong> our analytics, advertising, and hosting
          providers, and Amazon (only in the form of affiliate referral data, not
          your personal details).
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="use">
      <h2 id="use">How we use information</h2>
      <p>We use the information we collect to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Provide the timer and steeping guidance and keep the site working.
        </li>
        <li>
          Understand which guides and features are useful so we can improve them
          and fix what is confusing.
        </li>
        <li>Measure site traffic and performance through Google Analytics.</li>
        <li>
          Show relevant advertising through Google AdSense, including
          personalized ads based on your activity where permitted.
        </li>
        <li>Reply to your messages and provide support.</li>
        <li>
          Protect the site from abuse, errors, and fraud, and comply with legal
          obligations.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="legal-basis">
      <h2 id="legal-basis">Legal basis for processing (GDPR)</h2>
      <p>
        [⚠️ LEGAL REVIEW REQUIRED — the lawful bases below are a starting point
        and must be confirmed by a qualified attorney for your specific setup.]
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Consent:</strong> we rely on your consent for non-essential cookies,
          analytics, and personalized advertising (where required, such as in the
          EU/UK).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Legitimate interests:</strong> we rely on our legitimate interest
          in operating, securing, and improving a free public tool for analytics aggregated
          at the site level and for security.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Communication:</strong> we use information you send through our
          contact page or email to respond to your request.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Legal obligation:</strong> we may process data where the law requires
          it.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="sharing">
      <h2 id="sharing">Data sharing and third parties</h2>
      <p>We share information with a small set of service providers:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Google LLC</strong> — Google Analytics (usage measurement) and Google
          AdSense (advertising). Google processes this data under its own privacy
          policy. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
            >Google's Privacy Policy</a
          > and the <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/"
            >Google Ads Settings</a
          >.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Our hosting provider</strong> — website hosting and delivery.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Amazon Associates</strong> — affiliate links. Amazon tracks referrals
          under its own policy; we earn a commission on qualifying purchases.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Our contact channel</strong> — messages sent through our contact
          page or email so we can reply.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Legal authorities</strong> — where required by law or to protect
          our rights and users.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We do not sell your personal information for money. Note, however, that
        using personalized advertising through Google may be considered a "sale"
        or "sharing" of personal information under some US state laws (such as
        California's CPRA). You can opt out as described below.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="transfers">
      <h2 id="transfers">International data transfers</h2>
      <p>
        [⚠️ LEGAL REVIEW REQUIRED — our providers, including Google and Amazon,
        may process data in the United States and other countries. For users in
        the European Economic Area and the UK, such transfers rely on
        appropriate safeguards such as Standard Contractual Clauses and Google's
        certified protections. Confirm and describe the exact mechanisms with
        counsel.]
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="retention">
      <h2 id="retention">Data retention</h2>
      <p>
        [⚠️ LEGAL REVIEW REQUIRED — retention periods must be specific. As a
        starting point:]
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Analytics data is retained according to Google's settings (Google
          Analytics defaults to 14 months of activity before automatic
          deletion).
        </li>
        <li>
          Messages sent through our contact page or email are kept only as long
          as needed to handle your request, then deleted.
        </li>
        <li>
          Advertising and cookie data are handled under Google's retention
          terms.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="rights">
      <h2 id="rights">Your rights and choices</h2>
      <p>
        Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct,
        delete, or port your personal data, to object to or restrict certain
        processing, and to withdraw consent. [⚠️ LEGAL REVIEW REQUIRED — the
        exact rights and how to exercise them vary by jurisdiction (GDPR in the
        EU/UK, CCPA/CPRA in California, and other US state laws).]
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Analytics and advertising controls:</strong> you can manage or disable
          cookies through our consent controls (where shown) and through your browser.
          For Google, use the <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/"
            >Google Ads Settings</a
          > and <a href="https://myadcenter.google.com/">My Ad Center</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information:</strong> We use Google
          AdSense, whose personalized advertising may be considered a "sale" or "sharing"
          of personal information under California (CPRA) and similar US state laws.
          You can opt out through our
          <a href="#" class="do-not-sell-link" hidden data-do-not-sell>
            Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information
          </a> link, which opens Google's opt-out dialog for applicable US state residents.
          The link appears only where required by law.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Contact us:</strong> to exercise any right, use our <a
            href="/contact">Contact page</a
          > or email <a href="mailto:hello@timeremind.info"
            >hello@timeremind.info</a
          >. We will respond within the timeframe required by law.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="cookies">
      <h2 id="cookies">Cookies and tracking</h2>
      <p>We and our partners use cookies and similar technologies to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Operate the site</strong> (essential cookies).</li>
        <li><strong>Measure usage</strong> (Google Analytics).</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Show advertising</strong> (Google AdSense, including personalized
          ads).
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        In regions that require it (such as the EU and UK), we will ask for your
        consent before setting non-essential cookies for analytics and
        personalized advertising. [⚠️ LEGAL REVIEW REQUIRED — you must implement
        a compliant consent management platform (CMP) that blocks Google
        Analytics and personalized AdSense tags until consent is given. Google
        requires a CMP certified under the IAB Transparency &amp; Consent
        Framework (TCF) or an equivalent for personalized ads in these regions.]
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="affiliate">
      <h2 id="affiliate">Affiliate links</h2>
      <p>
        Time Reminder participates in the Amazon Associates program and other
        affiliate programs. Some links to products are affiliate links, which
        means we may earn a commission if you buy through them, at no extra cost
        to you. These links are editorial and are kept separate from steeping
        guidance so they never influence our recommendations. Amazon and any
        other retailer handles your purchase and data under its own privacy
        policy.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="security">
      <h2 id="security">Security</h2>
      <p>
        We use reasonable measures to protect information, including HTTPS
        encryption in transit, access controls, and reputable hosted
        infrastructure. No website can guarantee perfect security, and you use
        the site at your own risk.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="children">
      <h2 id="children">Children's privacy</h2>
      <p>
        Time Reminder is intended for general audiences and is not directed to
        children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from
        children. [⚠️ LEGAL REVIEW REQUIRED — if you later target users under 13
        or under 16 in the EU, additional compliance (such as COPPA or
        age-appropriate design rules) applies.]
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="changes">
      <h2 id="changes">Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy as our practices or the law change. If we make
        material changes, we will post the updated policy here and update the
        "Last updated" date. [⚠️ LEGAL REVIEW REQUIRED — decide whether material
        changes require advance notice or consent.]
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="contact">
      <h2 id="contact">Contact us</h2>
      <p>
        Questions or requests about this policy or your data: email
        <a href="/contact">Contact page</a> or email
        <a href="mailto:hello@timeremind.info">hello@timeremind.info</a>. For
        EU/UK users, you also have the right to lodge a complaint with your
        local data protection authority.
      </p>
      <p class="effective">Effective date: {lastUpdated}.</p>
    </section>

    <p class="disclaimer">
      This privacy policy is provided for informational purposes and is not
      legal advice. Have a qualified data-privacy attorney review it before
      publication, especially the sections marked for legal review.
    </p>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .privacy-page {
    max-width: 44rem;
  }
  .updated-note {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    margin-top: -0.5rem;
  }
  .privacy-page section {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }
  .privacy-page h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-playfair);
    font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 3vw, 1.75rem);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }
  .privacy-page h3 {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    margin: 1.25rem 0 0.4rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }
  .privacy-page p,
  .privacy-page li {
    color: var(--color-text);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .privacy-page ul {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem;
  }
  .privacy-page a {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }
  .privacy-page a:hover {
    color: var(--color-accent-hover);
  }
  .effective {
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .disclaimer {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 1rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
</style>
